From 341a8f5c0999cef276fda2009db0cd0158282750 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:53:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] model routing: live agents adopt the managed policy
 when enforcement is enabled; split aux/main allocation counters

Found while enabling subscription-only routing across the fleet:

1. Subscription provenance was minted only at agent construction, so every agent alive when
   an operator set model_routing.enforce_subscription_only (gateway-cached Slack/Desktop
   sessions, running Kanban workers) failed closed at its next request with "lacks verified
   subscription provenance". adopt_managed_policy() now re-resolves the live agent's own tuple
   as a managed exact pin before any request is shaped (_build_api_kwargs_for_mode and the
   attempt path), rebuilding its client from the fenced subscription runtime and dropping
   fallback chains. Unapproved tuples (OpenRouter, paid keys, unknown models) still raise
   before any send.

2. Main sessions and their auxiliary allocations shared one round-robin counter per class, so
   with two providers each session's main allocation always landed on the same provider (the
   paired aux call took the other). Aux owners (aux:<owner>:<task>:<class>) now keep their own
   counter; the main counter key is unchanged so existing positions survive.

Tests: tests/agent/test_managed_adoption.py (streaming + non-streaming adoption with OAuth-only
wire auth, unapproved pin fails closed with zero completion sends, no-op when unenforced, aux
counter split, main counter compatibility). RED without the fix; routing/managed/compression/
gateway suites 148 files / 1391 tests pass.
